        prompt: "A 3.0 m diving board of mass 30 kg is supported at one end by a pivot and 1.0 m along by a post. A 50 kg diver stands at the free end. Calculate the forces at the pivot and the post. (g = 9.81 m s⁻²)", marks: 5,
        scheme: ["Weights: board 294 N at 1.5 m; diver 490 N at 3.0 m", "Moments about the pivot: R_post×1.0 = 294×1.5 + 490×3.0 = 441+1470 = 1911 N", "Vertical balance: R_pivot = 294+490−1911 = −1127 N (pivot must hold the board down)", "So post pushes up ~1.9 kN, pivot pulls down ~1.1 kN"],
